WEBVTT

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:48.333
I don't need any friends or partners.

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:50.333
What are you talking about?! Even you--

00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:52.667
Stop concerning yourself with me!

00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:20.208
Kim, you're not <i>so </i>bad.

00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:25.125
Hmph. Don't get too full of yourself,
just because you're in EAT.

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:26.708
Huh?

00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:30.917
Wait, what was that?

00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:32.375
Why are you blushing?

00:01:32.375 --> 00:01:33.583
Why are <i>you</i>?

00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:34.792
You're turning red.

00:01:34.792 --> 00:01:35.958
I am not!

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:37.042
Yes you are.

00:01:37.042 --> 00:01:38.792
Geez!

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.125
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:47.958
You're... pretty, you know.

00:01:47.958 --> 00:01:49.500
Huh?

00:01:51.542 --> 00:01:53.458
Whoa...

00:02:00.542 --> 00:02:01.833
What was that?!

00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:04.958
No! It was just a dream, all right?!

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.917
Huh?

00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:14.208
<i>we wanna be there even if we had to</i>
<i>twist the world all around to get there</i>

00:02:14.208 --> 00:02:25.125
<i>without you, i guess i couldn't</i>
<i>even find the future here today</i>

00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:36.083
<i>i was always trying to take nothing for granted</i>

00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:44.083
<i>for the day i might lose them</i>

00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:51.125
<i>but you just came in to my black</i>
<i>and white monochrome destiny</i>

00:02:51.125 --> 00:03:01.292
<i>and colored it all over</i>

00:03:02.125 --> 00:03:08.708
<i>we won't be satisfied with the routine future</i>

00:03:08.708 --> 00:03:16.125
<i>we were born to make a new history come true</i>

00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:23.292
<i>there's absolutely no</i>
<i>absolute thing in this world</i>

00:03:23.292 --> 00:03:27.875
<i>this road goes on forever</i>

00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:34.000
<i>as long as we won't give up</i>

00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:39.292
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:03:39.292 --> 00:03:41.000
Tie, go again!

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.292
Look this way now!

00:03:43.292 --> 00:03:46.875
Ah, Tsugumi, that's no fair!

00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:51.000
--I couldn't help it!
--Coochie-coochie-coochie!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.125
What is this? Do you find that to be fun?

00:03:55.125 --> 00:03:56.833
Miss Anya, do you want to try?

00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:59.917
Why should I engage in such poor-man's play?

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.458
This is rock, scissors, and paper, see?

00:04:04.458 --> 00:04:08.458
I get that. I guess I have
no choice but to play along.

00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:11.125
I can handle myself in commoner games.

00:04:12.083 --> 00:04:14.958
--Rock, paper, scissors!
--Rock, paper, scissors!

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:22.708
What am I going to do

00:04:22.708 --> 00:04:27.250
about the urge to smack
commoners built up in my right hand?

00:04:29.792 --> 00:04:31.625
Hey, you guys!

00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:33.250
Kim, ma'am...

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.833
What's going on?

00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:36.708
Why the indecent outfit?

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:38.583
I found us a great job.

00:04:38.583 --> 00:04:39.958
Huh?

00:04:39.958 --> 00:04:42.458
Change into something
you don't mind getting wet.

00:04:42.583 --> 00:04:45.583
"Invitation Fighting!"

00:04:53.958 --> 00:04:56.167
Pool cleaning?

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.125
Yep! Any job where you can play in the water

00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:01.917
while making money is a
good one, right? It is hot, and all,

00:05:01.917 --> 00:05:04.167
so don't spend your time
rotting away in your room.

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:06.583
We aren't exactly <i>rotten</i>.

00:05:06.583 --> 00:05:08.292
Okay, it's all yours.

00:05:08.292 --> 00:05:12.458
Right! My associates will do their job!

00:05:12.458 --> 00:05:14.458
It's just like a summer teen drama, huh?

00:05:14.458 --> 00:05:15.917
What, pool cleaning?

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:17.292
And by the way...

00:05:17.292 --> 00:05:19.000
Well, shall we get started?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.833
What are<i> you </i>doing here, too?!

00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:24.000
Kim, you, me, and one other,
let's go get the cleaning gear.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.958
Why are you in charge?!

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:29.625
With just you folks, it will take
forever to finish this job, right?

00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:32.958
With me in charge,
things will proceed more efficiently.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.917
I'll let you handle the process,
but I'm still the leader, got it?

00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:42.875
Suit yourself.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:46.333
It's so dark, I can't tell where anything is.

00:05:48.875 --> 00:05:52.042
Come to think of it, you're a lantern, huh?

00:05:52.042 --> 00:05:55.500
How about it? I'm pretty handy, aren't I?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:59.833
Don't get that heat too close.
Shine it over there.

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:02.083
Tsugumi, let's find the cleaning gear.

00:06:02.083 --> 00:06:04.083
Uh, right.

00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:25.583
Gah! Tsugumi, I'll get you!

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.833
You too, Miss Anya!

00:06:33.542 --> 00:06:35.500
That looks like an expensive one-piece.

00:06:36.708 --> 00:06:39.208
Whoosh.

00:06:42.583 --> 00:06:44.167
What are you goofing around for?!

00:06:44.167 --> 00:06:45.500
Sorry.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.708
She's right! This is no time for games!

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:51.375
Good grief, straight-laced chick.

00:06:51.875 --> 00:06:54.083
Who cares if they goof around a little?

00:06:54.083 --> 00:06:56.375
You really are no fun.

00:06:56.375 --> 00:06:59.542
We should finish working
right away, and<i> then </i>play.

00:06:59.542 --> 00:07:04.167
I'm thinking about playing
around myself, after all.

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:08.458
In any case, it sucks to be
whoever has to partner up with you.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.750
Is there some problem?

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:18.667
Yes. Please look at this.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:24.083
This is that Traitor from the other day.

00:07:24.083 --> 00:07:28.708
The police currently have
him in custody as a suspect.

00:07:30.542 --> 00:07:32.125
He doesn't sleep.

00:07:32.125 --> 00:07:33.417
Doesn't sleep?

00:07:33.417 --> 00:07:38.000
I ran through his background,
but he has no criminal past,

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.417
nor does he have any martial arts
experience like the Traitors use.

00:07:41.417 --> 00:07:44.792
He was very much a normal, law-abiding citizen.

00:07:44.792 --> 00:07:49.417
I see. You're saying that the
man suddenly changed, then.

00:07:49.417 --> 00:07:52.042
He also displays the
abnormality of not sleeping.

00:07:52.042 --> 00:07:53.750
Yes.

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:57.792
There is a possibility that
witches are involved in this case.

00:07:57.792 --> 00:08:01.792
DWMA and witches are
longstanding mutual enemies.

00:08:01.792 --> 00:08:05.250
This could be some ill-begotten witch's scheme.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.708
DWMA will take on this case.

00:08:07.708 --> 00:08:11.708
I will see to it that arrangements
are made to transfer the suspect.

00:08:11.708 --> 00:08:13.625
Please be careful.

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:19.625
Understood. This isn't the same as
letting young witches stay at large.

00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:25.958
Kim, ma'am, we're done!

00:08:25.958 --> 00:08:30.417
O-Oh, yeah. Good work.

00:08:30.417 --> 00:08:31.792
It's so slick.

00:08:31.792 --> 00:08:33.542
We've accomplished our task!

00:08:33.542 --> 00:08:35.917
--Just like a teen drama, huh?
--You finished that pretty quickly, huh?

00:08:35.917 --> 00:08:37.875
--What is a teen drama, anyway?
--Here, your pay.

00:08:37.875 --> 00:08:38.583
--What is a teen drama, anyway?
--Thank you!

00:08:38.583 --> 00:08:41.875
--A teen drama, you see, is...
--Okay, I look forward to doing business again.

00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:47.750
Hey, associates! Here's your pay!

00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:52.500
Here, split that three ways.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.542
Huh? This is all?

00:08:54.542 --> 00:08:57.667
We haven't even done anything yet,
either. Thank you very much.

00:08:57.667 --> 00:08:59.583
We cleaned the pool.

00:08:59.583 --> 00:09:00.750
Huh?

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.917
This is a lot less than we
got working at the cafe, isn't it?

00:09:04.917 --> 00:09:07.500
Yes, a lot less.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.292
Mm-hmm, like candy from a baby.

00:09:10.292 --> 00:09:11.750
Kim...

00:09:14.375 --> 00:09:15.833
Uh, listen...

00:09:17.583 --> 00:09:20.167
Since we finished work so quickly and all,

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:24.208
I know this delicious ice cream shop,
so would you like to go?

00:09:24.208 --> 00:09:26.708
Huh? You're kidding, right?

00:09:26.708 --> 00:09:30.833
Why do I have to go anywhere
with a straight-laced chick like you?

00:09:30.833 --> 00:09:33.083
You couldn't even pay me to.

00:09:42.667 --> 00:09:46.250
Um, Jacqueline, ma'am?

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.250
What is it?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.458
Do you need something?

00:09:49.458 --> 00:09:53.208
Ma'am, by any chance...

00:09:53.208 --> 00:09:56.208
You want to partner up with Miss Kim, don't you?

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:01.917
W-W-What-- What are you talking about?!

00:10:01.917 --> 00:10:04.292
Please, let us help you!

00:10:04.292 --> 00:10:06.000
Huh?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.000
"Us"?

00:10:16.792 --> 00:10:20.417
What's the matter? Why are you
staring at the tanuki ornament?

00:10:20.417 --> 00:10:21.792
She's "Josephine."

00:10:21.792 --> 00:10:25.750
Oh, I was just thinking,
it reminds me a lot of like Miss Kim.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.083
It sure does.

00:10:27.083 --> 00:10:28.708
Pom poko-cize!

00:10:28.708 --> 00:10:32.833
You'll get killed if you
ever say that to Miss Kim.

00:10:32.833 --> 00:10:34.625
Pom poko-cide!

00:10:34.625 --> 00:10:37.167
Huh? A compatibility reading?

00:10:37.167 --> 00:10:40.917
Yes. Miss Kana's fortune
telling is extremely accurate.

00:10:40.917 --> 00:10:43.792
No matter how much you stick on Miss Kim,

00:10:43.792 --> 00:10:47.125
there isn't any point if you aren't compatible.

00:10:47.125 --> 00:10:49.667
What a surprisingly severe thing to say.

00:10:49.667 --> 00:10:51.625
Okay, let's go.

00:10:55.292 --> 00:10:58.000
I will now read your love life.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.333
Are you sure this is accurate?

00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:05.375
"Embankment"
[<i>dote</i>: embankment]

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:09.625
"Embankment-pumpkin." [<i>Dotekabocha</i>: a pumpkin
unfit for eating; a fat, ugly, worthless girl]

00:11:09.625 --> 00:11:10.958
What did you say?! [<i>Dotekabocha</i>: a pumpkin
unfit for eating; a fat, ugly, worthless girl]

00:11:10.958 --> 00:11:14.375
--You're--hey! How can you say anything so rude!
--Okay, okay, this way, Miss Anya.

00:11:14.375 --> 00:11:16.125
Everything is all right.

00:11:16.125 --> 00:11:18.875
Miss Kana, please begin at once.

00:11:21.375 --> 00:11:24.958
Imagine the person whose
compatibility you want to have read,

00:11:24.958 --> 00:11:26.333
and pick a card.

00:11:26.333 --> 00:11:28.667
Huh? Imagine them?

00:11:33.292 --> 00:11:34.958
Go ahead.

00:11:41.375 --> 00:11:43.333
The Lovers.

00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:44.958
You're a perfect match.

00:11:44.958 --> 00:11:47.958
Isn't that great, Jacqueline, ma'am?

00:11:49.333 --> 00:11:52.625
Guys, I found it!

00:11:52.625 --> 00:11:55.333
The surefire way to land Miss Kim!

00:12:00.167 --> 00:12:01.708
Rolled omelets?

00:12:01.708 --> 00:12:02.833
Yes.

00:12:02.833 --> 00:12:07.333
I got this information from one of
Miss Kim's underground stalkers--

00:12:07.333 --> 00:12:12.208
members of her fan club,
so I think it's pretty accurate.

00:12:14.958 --> 00:12:17.542
The private eye character in
"The Commoner of Flanders"

00:12:17.542 --> 00:12:19.708
has to be Miss Kim Diehl, huh?

00:12:20.375 --> 00:12:22.708
What an adorable favorite food to have.

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.750
Using her favorite food to lure her in?

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:29.000
Miss Kim does act like a tanuki,
so this just might work.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:32.958
But I'm not sure I can make a very good omelet.

00:12:32.958 --> 00:12:35.208
In that case, leave it to me!

00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:41.667
Whenever my mom was busy at home,

00:12:41.667 --> 00:12:44.458
I would make bento lunches
for my dad and brother,

00:12:44.458 --> 00:12:46.292
so I'm pretty good at simple cooking.

00:12:46.292 --> 00:12:47.375
Oh!

00:12:47.375 --> 00:12:50.917
Oh, my, Miss Tsugumi,
you get high points, don't you?

00:12:50.917 --> 00:12:54.917
You're so wholehearted,
and you'd be quite a catch as a wife.

00:12:55.583 --> 00:12:56.792
Oh, yeah?

00:12:56.792 --> 00:13:00.250
"Wholehearted," despite not
being able to pick a partner yet?

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.583
Love and picking partners
are two different matters!

00:13:02.583 --> 00:13:04.250
That's right! It's different!

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.333
Huh?

00:13:05.333 --> 00:13:09.958
But Jacqueline, ma'am, why is it
you want to partner with Miss Kim?

00:13:09.958 --> 00:13:13.500
Huh? Hmm...

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.333
Yes, why...?

00:13:16.333 --> 00:13:20.625
When she's on my mind,
I think I'd like to be with her.

00:13:20.625 --> 00:13:24.958
Could this be what love is?
Is it because Kim is so boyish?

00:13:24.958 --> 00:13:30.375
No, Kim is more glamorous than I am,
and we're both girls anyway...

00:13:31.417 --> 00:13:34.250
Wait, what am I thinking?!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.292
Jacqueline, ma'am, you're on fire!

00:13:36.292 --> 00:13:37.292
Just like a lantern!

00:13:37.292 --> 00:13:38.792
Water! Water!

00:13:38.792 --> 00:13:40.875
No! If you were to pour water on her...

00:13:40.875 --> 00:13:42.208
Then a damp towel?

00:13:42.208 --> 00:13:43.458
She's going to die!

00:13:43.458 --> 00:13:45.083
Those are the flames of love.

00:13:45.083 --> 00:13:46.667
I'm not in love!

00:13:56.042 --> 00:13:57.667
They turned out well, didn't they?

00:13:57.667 --> 00:14:02.458
Leave it to a lantern to know
how to handle the heat so well.

00:14:02.458 --> 00:14:04.417
Oh, rolled omelets?

00:14:04.417 --> 00:14:06.417
Ah, Kim, ma'am...

00:14:07.792 --> 00:14:09.792
Would you like one?

00:14:09.792 --> 00:14:12.292
Miss Jacqueline made them.

00:14:12.292 --> 00:14:16.250
Oh, yeah? Well then, I'll take one.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.333
That's one that I made.

00:14:18.333 --> 00:14:20.042
Huh?

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:25.875
Why, you... straight-laced chick!

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:31.167
Actually, the most important
thing for a woman is her looks!

00:14:31.167 --> 00:14:32.083
Her looks?

00:14:32.083 --> 00:14:34.958
From "Operation: Show Off Your Pretty Hair" to

00:14:34.958 --> 00:14:37.958
"Operation: Casual
Conversation in the Bathroom."

00:15:02.458 --> 00:15:05.375
It seems especially crowded in here today, huh?

00:15:12.708 --> 00:15:15.625
Ma'am, your hair is so pretty,

00:15:15.625 --> 00:15:20.208
but what is the difference between
rinse, conditioner, and treatment?

00:15:20.208 --> 00:15:24.042
A rinse coats the hair's surface,
protecting it from friction,

00:15:24.042 --> 00:15:25.875
and makes it feel smooth.

00:15:25.875 --> 00:15:28.833
Conditioner is better at keeping
the hair's surface manageable

00:15:28.833 --> 00:15:30.458
than a rinse is.

00:15:30.458 --> 00:15:33.333
A treatment has the
same effect that a rinse does,

00:15:33.333 --> 00:15:35.917
but in addition, it also
treats the inside of the hair.

00:15:35.917 --> 00:15:38.917
I use a treatment every day.

00:15:38.917 --> 00:15:40.917
Wow! I can't remember all that!

00:15:40.917 --> 00:15:44.208
Jacqueline, ma'am, we're going to
be pretty by being friends with you!

00:15:44.208 --> 00:15:46.375
And we'll get shiny cuticles, too!

00:15:46.375 --> 00:15:49.000
Looks are important, even for commoners!

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:53.042
What is this? You ragging on
my short hair, or something?

00:15:56.292 --> 00:15:59.125
Aren't you going to soak in the tub?

00:15:59.125 --> 00:16:03.958
You guys are making too
much racket, so I'm outta here!

00:16:03.958 --> 00:16:06.333
Miss Kim is one mean tanuki!

00:16:08.917 --> 00:16:10.792
The Fool.

00:16:10.792 --> 00:16:13.000
Girls just love anniversaries!

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:15.958
When someone remembers your
anniversary, and gives you a present,

00:16:15.958 --> 00:16:17.708
it makes you happy, doesn't it?

00:16:17.708 --> 00:16:20.708
It would be more convincing coming
from someone besides you, Miss Meme.

00:16:20.708 --> 00:16:22.500
Yeah, sure, whatever.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.625
Eternal Feather, ma'am...

00:16:24.625 --> 00:16:25.958
Leave it to me!

00:16:28.917 --> 00:16:30.000
What's this?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.125
Miss Kim's top-secret information.

00:16:32.125 --> 00:16:34.417
Is this from that fan club, too?

00:16:34.417 --> 00:16:36.000
Yes.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.958
Oh... It has her favorite color
and all sorts of things.

00:16:38.958 --> 00:16:40.917
154 cm tall.

00:16:40.917 --> 00:16:45.125
Her measurements are 81-56-79!

00:16:45.125 --> 00:16:47.125
Nice body.

00:16:47.125 --> 00:16:50.250
Huh? Doesn't this seem odd? Her birthday--

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:53.208
it's April 31st.

00:16:53.208 --> 00:16:55.958
April only goes up to the 30th, right?

00:16:55.958 --> 00:17:00.208
This isn't going to work.
Her all-important birthday is in doubt.

00:17:00.208 --> 00:17:03.375
I wouldn't be surprised if
Miss Kim doesn't remember it, either.

00:17:03.375 --> 00:17:05.333
Miss Meme, she isn't you.

00:17:08.292 --> 00:17:11.458
I'm going to go ask around
to the others in the girls' dorm.

00:17:11.458 --> 00:17:12.500
Okay, I'll come with you.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:13.875
I'm coming, too.

00:17:15.625 --> 00:17:18.875
I thought the witch of the
girls' dorm came from Spain.

00:17:18.875 --> 00:17:20.542
She was born in Brazil, right?

00:17:20.542 --> 00:17:23.083
I'd heard it was Tunisia.

00:17:23.083 --> 00:17:25.292
She's an aspiring actress, right?

00:17:25.292 --> 00:17:27.250
No she's not, she's a gang member.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.000
She's an alien.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:32.667
Well, I've never spoken to her. Sorry.

00:17:35.042 --> 00:17:37.500
This is all messed up.

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:40.583
Seems like she's hiding her background.

00:17:40.583 --> 00:17:42.542
Let's stop prying, already.

00:17:42.542 --> 00:17:44.625
--Huh?
--Huh? But...

00:17:44.625 --> 00:17:49.875
Kim is who she is. Sneaking around
won't get me any closer to her.

00:17:49.875 --> 00:17:54.250
I want Kim to feel my soul.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:58.875
So I have to be the one
to first run into her, head-on!

00:18:00.167 --> 00:18:03.208
You don't have anything to lose anymore.

00:18:03.208 --> 00:18:06.125
And that's because of us, isn't it?

00:18:06.125 --> 00:18:10.125
That's okay. Thanks. I'll go find Kim.

00:18:14.458 --> 00:18:17.333
It looks like DWMA is making its move.

00:18:17.333 --> 00:18:20.250
We've collected a fair
amount of experimental data.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:25.792
But it's still too soon.
Let's cover our tracks, just to be safe.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:34.833
Witches are the total enemy of DWMA.
I cannot afford to be found.

00:18:34.833 --> 00:18:38.917
I must conceal my past to live.

00:18:38.917 --> 00:18:44.583
But that is just for now.
A witch's instinct is for destruction.

00:18:44.583 --> 00:18:48.583
I'll teach them a lesson in
the despair and loneliness

00:18:48.583 --> 00:18:50.792
that I've experienced up to now.

00:19:02.583 --> 00:19:06.292
I wasn't born a witch
because I wanted to be one.

00:19:12.625 --> 00:19:14.500
Go away!

00:19:19.958 --> 00:19:23.333
Don't go throwing me in
with a stray dog like you!

00:19:25.292 --> 00:19:27.542
I'm by myself because I wanna be.

00:19:48.333 --> 00:19:50.958
Just hold on! I'll heal you up right away!

00:20:14.625 --> 00:20:17.000
Hey!

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.958
Cut that out!

00:20:18.958 --> 00:20:23.375
Wow. You healed his injuries.

00:20:23.375 --> 00:20:26.875
Was that... magic?

00:20:28.583 --> 00:20:29.667
No.

00:20:29.667 --> 00:20:31.333
But that puppy was definitely--

00:20:31.333 --> 00:20:33.375
It wasn't! This was just...

00:20:33.375 --> 00:20:38.417
Are you, by any chance... a real witch?

00:20:39.958 --> 00:20:43.708
But how? How can that be?

00:20:43.708 --> 00:20:47.083
It's not like I was born a witch
because I wanted to be one.

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:51.333
I hated the world of witches, and ran away.

00:20:51.333 --> 00:20:56.708
I thought that if I was at DWMA,
I could cut my ties to being a witch.

00:20:56.708 --> 00:21:02.750
I even cut my prized hair,
dressed like a boy, and avoided others,

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:04.042
but then, out of all people,

00:21:04.042 --> 00:21:07.833
why did a straight-laced chick
like you have to be the one?

00:21:07.833 --> 00:21:11.083
Kim, are you...

00:21:11.083 --> 00:21:12.750
I'm finished.

00:21:20.375 --> 00:21:21.125
Let me go!

00:21:21.125 --> 00:21:22.000
No way!

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.750
Stop it! What do you want?!

00:21:26.292 --> 00:21:28.958
It's all right!

00:21:28.958 --> 00:21:31.250
It's all right.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:36.708
Since I'm a straight-laced chick,
like you say, I can keep a secret.

00:21:36.708 --> 00:21:41.042
You idiot. There's no way I can believe you...

00:21:41.042 --> 00:21:44.667
Okay then, as hush money,
you can buy me something.

00:21:44.667 --> 00:21:46.125
Huh?

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:52.375
I know this delicious ice cream shop.

00:21:52.375 --> 00:21:53.875
Okay...

00:21:57.375 --> 00:21:59.125
Yum!

00:21:59.125 --> 00:22:02.833
Why are those three
idiots here, too? Money is tight.

00:22:02.833 --> 00:22:06.958
Well, Kim, ma'am, you shortchanged
us on our pay earlier, didn't you?

00:22:06.958 --> 00:22:08.958
What was that?! You've got a smart mouth!

00:22:08.958 --> 00:22:09.875
Let's get another.

00:22:09.875 --> 00:22:10.583
Hey!

00:22:10.583 --> 00:22:14.458
--That sounds good.
--I wanted to come here alone with Kim.

00:22:14.458 --> 00:22:19.333
However, I now know that
my feelings toward Kim aren't love.

00:22:20.958 --> 00:22:24.750
That thing earlier is just
between the two of us.

00:22:29.583 --> 00:22:33.042
Your only saving grace is
that you're so straight-laced,

00:22:33.042 --> 00:22:35.583
so make sure you hold up your end.

00:22:35.583 --> 00:22:39.250
From now on, you're gonna
be my partner, after all.

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:41.500
Huh? You mean...

00:22:43.667 --> 00:22:45.333
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm!

00:22:47.542 --> 00:22:51.708
<i>With a big wave and a "See you,"</i>

00:22:51.708 --> 00:22:58.625
<i>let's meet in the new day</i>

00:23:15.375 --> 00:23:19.542
<i>Our shadows stretch along the pavement</i>

00:23:19.542 --> 00:23:23.542
<i>coming together, then apart, then together</i>

00:23:23.542 --> 00:23:31.875
<i>What do I say when the road home ends?</i>

00:23:31.875 --> 00:23:36.042
<i>You are not alone. Nope, right nearby,</i>

00:23:36.042 --> 00:23:40.167
<i>there are eyes looking back at you</i>

00:23:40.167 --> 00:23:44.292
<i>And just like a miracle,</i>

00:23:44.292 --> 00:23:48.042
<i>they can turn even failures into laughter</i>

00:23:48.042 --> 00:23:52.167
<i>Thank you for a fun day</i>

00:23:52.167 --> 00:23:56.500
<i>Let's do it again tomorrow</i>

00:23:56.500 --> 00:24:00.583
<i>We'll open a brand-new door</i>

00:24:00.583 --> 00:24:04.750
<i>chasing after dreams and love</i>

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:10.375
<i>and those nameless feelings, too</i>

00:24:18.083 --> 00:24:20.958
Two devils appear at Deathbucks Caffe.

00:24:20.958 --> 00:24:23.583
My special place is being taken away from me.

00:24:23.583 --> 00:24:25.833
I won't give in! I am a weapon, after all!

00:24:25.833 --> 00:24:27.042
Napolitan for me!

00:24:27.042 --> 00:24:28.917
Today's lunch special, please.

00:24:28.917 --> 00:24:32.278
"Next time: This is a Real Fight!"
One pilaf, please!
